ASTRA LAUNCHER — COMPLETE PRODUCT, UX AND SYSTEM EXPERIENCE REBUILD

The current build has made progress on the Android launcher foundation, but the product experience is still unacceptable.

Do NOT treat the current implementation as the finished Astra experience.

The current problem is not simply whether Astra technically launches applications.

The problem is that Astra currently feels like a raw prototype with an outdated launcher UX, weak visual design, primitive app discovery, excessive command-oriented interactions, poor Home experience, insufficient setup, and inadequate customization.

We are rebuilding the actual Astra product experience on top of the now-working real Android launcher foundation.

The goal is:

ASTRA SHOULD FEEL LIKE A PREMIUM PHONE ENVIRONMENT

Astra should feel like a complete, intentional Home environment.

It should not feel like:

- a normal Android application
- a command-line launcher
- an A-Z application list
- a developer prototype
- a settings demo
- an AI chatbot pretending to be a launcher
- a collection of disconnected screens

The experience should combine the strongest principles of:

- Apple iOS
- Samsung One UI
- Google Pixel
- Nothing OS

WITHOUT copying any of them.

Astra must have its own identity.

The design target is:

